# Deny by default: this directory tracks its own configuration and
# documentation -- `.gitignore`, `README.md`, `bitcoin.conf` -- and
# nothing else lives under version control here. Everything else this
# directory ever holds is Bitcoin Core's own runtime state: blocks,
# chainstate, indexes, wallets, logs, peer and ban lists, and mainnet's
# own siblings under `testnet3/`, `testnet4/` and `regtest/`. Naming
# those one at a time is a copy of another project's internals, and it
# goes stale the moment Core's own layout gains a file nobody here has
# added a line for -- the gap is silent, because `git status` shows an
# unlisted runtime file as an ordinary untracked file rather than as a
# defect in this file. Denying by default inverts the failure: a
# runtime artifact this file has never heard of is ignored on sight,
# and a file that belongs here but is missing from the negations
# below shows up as absent from `git ls-files` the first time anybody
# looks, rather than as a gap an enumeration cannot announce.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/bitcoin.conf
